 "final_message": "All twelve items are done, and the tests pass (6 passed, including the two new ones). I didn't write tests for the other fixes, so those are only covered by the existing tests.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** I changed `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` to follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added tests for the `None` rule in section 1 and the duplicate-id rule in section 5.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `flags_in_window` entry now says the last `days` entries (it used to say `days + 1`). I added a `daily_flag_counts` entry and noted in the `dedupe_transcripts` entry that the last duplicate is kept.\n- **Item 12:** The rest of the package also had bugs, which I fixed:\n  - `top_flagged_groups` didn't exclude empty groups or break ties by name.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` didn't map empty groups to `None` or sort its keys.\n  - `longest_positive_streak` never reset the run on a zero day.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `flagged` field other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_transcript_log` raise `ValueError` naming the line number for any other value, rather than guessing.",
